<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chilean War of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1810">1810</a>–<a href="/years/1826">1826</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-wars-of-independence">Spanish American wars of independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chilean War of Independence was the struggle of Chilean patriots against Spanish royalist rule, from the first national junta of 1810 to the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiloe">Chiloé</a> in 1826. After royalist forces reconquered Chile in 1814, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-the-andes">Army of the Andes</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-san-martin">José de San Martín</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernardo-ohiggins">Bernardo O'Higgins</a> crossed the mountains, won at Chacabuco (1817) and Maipú (1818), and independence was declared in 1818.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chilean-war-of-independence.jpg" alt="Chilean War of Independence" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan E. Casanova P · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Captura-de-Chilo%C3%A9.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
